Part 2: Database Design
Proposed Schema

company (
  id BIGINT PK,
  name VARCHAR,
  created_at TIMESTAMP
)

warehouse (
  id BIGINT PK,
  company_id BIGINT FK,
  name VARCHAR,
  location VARCHAR
)

product (
  id BIGINT PK,
  sku VARCHAR UNIQUE,
  name VARCHAR,
  price DECIMAL(10,2),
  product_type VARCHAR
)

inventory (
  id BIGINT PK,
  product_id BIGINT FK,
  warehouse_id BIGINT FK,
  quantity INT,
  UNIQUE(product_id, warehouse_id)
)

supplier (
  id BIGINT PK,
  name VARCHAR,
  contact_email VARCHAR
)
inventory_audit (
  id BIGINT PK,
  inventory_id BIGINT FK,
  previous_quantity INT,
  new_quantity INT,
  changed_at TIMESTAMP
)
product_supplier (
  product_id BIGINT FK,
  supplier_id BIGINT FK
)
product_bundle (
  parent_product_id BIGINT FK,
  child_product_id BIGINT FK,
  quantity INT
)

Design Justification

Separate inventory enables multi-warehouse support

Audit table ensures traceability

Unique constraints prevent duplication

Bundle table supports composite products

Indexed foreign keys improve performance
